UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 4, Week 3, Lesson 2: Building a food web', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"A food web connects overlapping food chains when animals eat more than one food or are eaten by more than one predator.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same science idea to a new object or material, then compare two pieces of evidence for strength.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nWhy is a food web often a better model of a real habitat than a single chain?\n\nFEEDBACK\nReal animals usually have more than one food or predator link; webs show those overlaps.\n\nWATCH FOR\nDrawing a web with no producers leaves consumers with nothing to start from.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nBuild a food web with at least eight organisms and twelve arrows. Trace two different chains inside the web and write what happens if one producer declines.\n\nWrite a short reflection naming one observation or step you corrected and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"Science and Technology","learning_intention":"A food web connects overlapping food chains when animals eat more than one food or are eaten by more than one predator.","lesson_number":2,"lesson_role":"Apply and make","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil","Optional: safe everyday objects for observation"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["ST2-SCI-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Build a food web with at least eight organisms and twelve arrows. Trace two different chains inside the web and write what happens if one producer declines. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Sample: new object/context, two named observations, claim about food web linked to that evidence.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Sample misconception: Drawing a web with no producers leaves consumers with nothing to start from.. Correction: Real animals usually have more than one food or predator link; with evidence.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Drawing a web with no producers leaves consumers with nothing to start from. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Investigate or describe a fresh example (not the worked objects) that uses food web. Record evidence and explain how it supports your claim.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Name one science misconception about food web, correct it with evidence, and say why the correction works.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Accept a new example with named observations and a claim–evidence link about food web. Reject title-only labels with no observation. / Accept a misconception plus corrected claim and evidence reason for food web. Reject wording changes that leave the same error..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"This matches the taught method for food web. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Drawing a web with no producers leaves consumers with nothing to start from","A claim that names no evidence from the lesson material","A method that skips the key step taught in this lesson","Real animals usually have more than one food or predator link"],"question":"Why is a food web often a better model of a real habitat than a single chain?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"This is the misconception to avoid for food web; the other choices align with the lesson method. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Real animals usually have more than one food or predator link","Careful use of link and explain why it matters with clear evidence","Drawing a web with no producers leaves consumers with nothing to start from","A food web connects overlapping food chains when animals eat more than one food or are eaten by more than one predator"],"question":"Which statement is a common mistake when working with food web?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Understanding is shown by new evidence and a named link and explain why it matters, not by copying the model. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Name link and explain why it matters only, without linking it to food web","Apply food web to new material and name the link and explain why it matters used","Repeat the worked example wording with no new evidence","Drawing a web with no producers leaves consumers with nothing to start from"],"question":"Which response best applies food web with new evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Trustworthy science claims rest on observable evidence linked to the claim. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Use observable features or measurements as evidence, not appearance alone","Decide from which object looks most exciting","Copy a label from the lesson title with no observation","Drawing a web with no producers leaves consumers with nothing to start from"],"question":"New examples: steam from a kettle, a germinating bean, a plastic dinosaur, a granite pebble. Which claim about food web is most trustworthy?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Science claims need named observations linked to the claim. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["A named observation plus how it supports the claim","A longer story with no observation","A label copied from the title with no evidence","Drawing a web with no producers leaves consumers with nothing to start from"],"question":"Which record best supports a science claim about food web?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"The strongest choice applies the taught idea about food web with evidence. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Change several conditions at once so something happens faster","Ignore measurements and decide by which looks nicer","Real animals usually have more than one food or predator link","Drawing a web with no producers leaves consumers with nothing to start from"],"question":"Using this science idea — A food web connects overlapping food chains when animals eat more than one food or are eaten by — which choice is strongest?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Fair tests change one variable, control the rest, and use recorded evidence. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Change one variable and keep the other conditions the same","Change several conditions at once so something happens faster","Stop early when you like the first result","Ignore measurements and decide by which looks nicer"],"question":"Which investigation design best tests an idea about food web?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Scientific predictions stay open to new observations rather than protecting a first guess. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Any exciting story about the object must be true","Drawing a web with no producers leaves consumers with nothing to start from","Results that disagree with the first guess should be discarded","If the observed feature changes, the claim about food web should change with it"],"question":"Which prediction about food web can be checked with evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence on new material demonstrates the skill; copying the model does not.","marking_guide":"Accept a new example with named observations and a claim–evidence link about food web. Reject title-only labels with no observation.","question":"Investigate or describe a fresh example (not the worked objects) that uses food web. Record evidence and explain how it supports your claim.","sample_answer":"Sample: new object/context, two named observations, claim about food web linked to that evidence.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A useful correction changes the inaccurate idea or method and explains why.","marking_guide":"Accept a misconception plus corrected claim and evidence reason for food web. Reject wording changes that leave the same error.","question":"Name one science misconception about food web, correct it with evidence, and say why the correction works.","sample_answer":"Sample misconception: Drawing a web with no producers leaves consumers with nothing to start from.. Correction: Real animals usually have more than one food or predator link; with evidence.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent evidence and reflection, with reasons where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-sci-y4-w03-l2","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA Science and Technology alignment using catalogue outcome codes; content-point mapping remains pending.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise food web.","Read the mission before you start observing or testing.","Keep the property or variable you are studying in view."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your evidence with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not match the method."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the observation or step that carries the idea.","Then write the reason without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore observations or fair tests.","Prefer accurate evidence over a guess that merely looks neat."],"submit":["Confirm that your evidence and reason are both present.","Proofread labels, measurements and sequence of steps.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title and find the worked model.","Name one exact observation or test step before you decide.","Try the small prompt before opening the comparison."],"teach1":["Return to the model and list the key observations.","Say what each observation shows about the idea.","A final label alone is weaker than recorded evidence."],"teach2":["Compare a weak claim with stronger evidence.","Change the claim or method, not only how neat the drawing looks.","Name the mistake you are repairing."],"teach3":["Choose a fresh object or context that still uses the same skill.","Write one reason in your own words.","Do not retype the worked model as your answer."],"write":["Follow every part of the independent instructions.","Include original evidence and a short reason.","Save work that shows the skill on new objects or data."]},"subject":"Living World","success_criteria":["I can use food web with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify link and explain why it matters.","I can practise overlap independently on a new prompt.","I can notice ecosystem needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"A food web connects overlapping food chains when animals eat more than one food or are eaten by more than one predator.","options":["A guess with no evidence","A claim unrelated to the observation or test","A food web connects overlapping food chains when animals eat more than one food or are eaten by more than one predator","An answer copied without understanding"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about food web with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nIn a pond web, a frog may eat insects and be eaten by a bird or snake. Multiple arrows show many feeding links, not one line.\n\nTRY FIRST\nWhy is a food web often a better model of a real habitat than a single chain?\n\nFEEDBACK\nReal animals usually have more than one food or predator link; webs show those overlaps.","explain":"A food web connects overlapping food chains when animals eat more than one food or are eaten by more than one predator.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner base claims on observation, fair tests and design evidence, rather than guessing from a picture alone. Keep every claim linked to what was seen or measured.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the observations, properties or test steps that carry the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your record with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your evidence? If a result is uncertain, identify what would have to be observed or tested again. One deliberate, evidence-based revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Drawing a web with no producers leaves consumers with nothing to start from. Correct the claim or method, not just the neatness of the diagram.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Food web model.","caption":"Include producers.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Web</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">overlapping chains</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Many links</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">one animal many foods</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which observation matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the observations, properties or test steps that carry the idea before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this model: In a pond web, a frog may eat insects and be eaten by a bird or snake. Multiple arrows show many feeding links, not one  Then write your own evidence.","who":"juno"}]}],"title":"Talk through the first model","transcript":"Pip: I can see the example, but I am not sure which observation matters most.\nJuno: Name the observations, properties or test steps that carry the idea before you decide.\nPip: I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.\nJuno: Pause here. Use this model: In a pond web, a frog may eat insects and be eaten by a bird or snake. Multiple arrows show many feeding links, not one  Then write your own evidence."}}]},{"check":{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Make the science idea visible: name the observation, source or example you used and say why it supports the claim.","options":["Make the science idea visible: name the observation, source or example you used and say why it supports the claim","A claim unrelated to the observation or test","An answer copied without understanding","A guess with no evidence"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about food web with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nIn a pond web, a frog may eat insects and be eaten by a bird or snake. Multiple arrows show many feeding links, not one line. Look at each observation, source detail or example that carries the idea.\n\nTRY FIRST\nList the key observations, sources or steps from the model and say what each one shows.\n\nFEEDBACK\nThe most useful record names the evidence and the reason it supports the claim, not only a label.","explain":"Make the science idea visible: name the observation, source or example you used and say why it supports the claim.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner base claims on observation, fair tests and design evidence, rather than guessing from a picture alone. Keep every claim linked to what was seen or measured.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the observations, properties or test steps that carry the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your record with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your evidence? If a result is uncertain, identify what would have to be observed or tested again. One deliberate, evidence-based revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Writing only a final label without evidence does not show science thinking. Correct the claim or method, not just the neatness of the diagram.","title":"Show the evidence","visual":[{"alt":"Overlaps vs producer-free web.","caption":"Eight+ organisms.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Trace two chains</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">inside web</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Risk</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">web with no plants</text></g></svg>"}]},{"check":{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Use an intentionally incorrect claim as a comparison.","options":["Use an intentionally incorrect claim as a comparison","A claim unrelated to the observation or test","An answer copied without understanding","A guess with no evidence"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about food web with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nDrawing a web with no producers leaves consumers with nothing to start from. Here is a more productive model: In a pond web, a frog may 